user_template:
Estimate editorial news importance for a broad audience following AI, not just engineering usefulness.

Score the underlying news conveyed by the title, supplied body and any quoted text together. Brevity is not absence of news: a concrete rollout, a consequential public statement, a meaningful research/capability claim, or a useful actionable technique can carry substantial news in one sentence. A prominent person's position in a live safety/policy/industry debate can itself be the news; it need not be a technical release. Conversely, density and technical detail alone do not make a narrow paper, integration or routine feature consequential.

Calibration:
- 0–19: essentially no identifiable news: pure reaction, greeting, empty praise or aesthetic caption.
- 20–39: limited-scope demonstrations/promotion, small tips, minor features, ordinary integrations, narrow incremental material.
- 40–59: concrete product/model/workflow developments, useful practical guidance, substantive research, identifiable industry discussion or notable first-party announcements/statements.
- 60–79: consequential releases or research, major capability claims, strategic investment, significant safety/legal/policy/economic developments or reports with broad effects.
- 80–100: exceptional, field-changing events or breakthroughs.
Choose intermediate integer scores rather than mechanically choosing range midpoints. These are evidence guides, not quotas.

Use source/author context to interpret what the item reports; a prestigious source alone is not enough. Do not add up all topics in a digest into a breakthrough score. Do not penalize a reported model version or event because it postdates your knowledge, or demand independent verification you cannot perform. Do not assume unseen linked content; a named concrete event remains evidence even if the short item lacks technical detail. Keep generic excitement distinct from an actual identified announcement. Judge contemporaneously with the supplied publication period.

Source tier: {{ item.tier }}
Source id: {{ item.source_id }}
Title: {{ item.title }}
Author: {{ item.author or "unknown" }}
Published: {{ item.published_at }}
URL: {{ item.url }}

Content:
{{ item.content_text[:5000] }}

Output:
```json
{
  "reason": "What news is actually conveyed and why it merits this importance, <=200 chars",
  "score": 0
}
```
score must be an integer from 0 to 100.
